{
  "id": "26556_toku",
  "headword": "{溶|と}く",
  "reading": "とく",
  "romaji": "toku",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to dissolve; to mix into a liquid",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to dissolve; to mix (a powder or solid) into a liquid",
      "explanation": "To stir or blend a substance into liquid until it dissolves or forms a smooth mixture. Commonly used in cooking for mixing ingredients like flour, eggs, or seasonings into liquid."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "26556_toku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{卵|たまご}を{溶|と}く。",
      "english": "Beat the eggs.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26556_toku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{味噌|みそ}を{湯|ゆ}に{溶|と}いてください。",
      "english": "Please dissolve the miso in the hot water.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "26556_toku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{小麦粉|こむぎこ}を{水|みず}で{溶|と}いてから、{少|すこ}しずつ{鍋|なべ}に{加|くわ}える。",
      "english": "Dissolve the flour in water, then gradually add it to the pot.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A godan verb used primarily in cooking to describe mixing a powder, paste, or solid into a liquid. The transitive counterpart of {溶|と}ける (to dissolve on its own).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし})\n- Pair: {溶|と}ける (intransitive — to dissolve, to melt)\n- Pattern: Xを{溶|と}く, Xを{水|みず}で{溶|と}く\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- Type: Telic (has endpoint)\n- {溶|と}いている: in the process of dissolving/mixing\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {卵|たまご}を{溶|と}く: to beat eggs\n- {味噌|みそ}を{溶|と}く: to dissolve miso\n- {小麦粉|こむぎこ}を{溶|と}く: to dissolve flour\n- {絵|え}の{具|ぐ}を{溶|と}く: to dilute paint\n\nNOTE ON HOMOPHONES:\nNot to be confused with {解|と}く (to solve, to untie) or {説|と}く (to explain, to preach), which have the same reading but different meanings and kanji.",
